---
title: Lazy Podi
tags:
    - podi
    - half-yearly
    - accoutrement
---


Heat 1 tsp of the @gingelly oil{2%tbsp} in a #pan. Roast the @solid hing (asafoetida){5%cubes} until it swells on all sides and becomes soft enough to crush with a spoon.

Add the @dried Kashmiri chillies{1%cup} and roast until crisp and fragrant, without letting them blacken. Transfer everything to a #plate and leave it to cool.

In the same pan, heat another teaspoon of the gingelly oil. Roast the @urad dal{1%cup} and @chana dal{2%tbsp} until the urad dal turns a deep rust-brown. Set aside to cool.

Now roast the @coconut, freshly grated{2.5%cups} and @curry leaves{1%cup} over medium heat, stirring continuously. Coconut can go from golden to burnt very quickly, so stay close. Once evenly brown, set it aside and let everything cool completely.

Grind the hing and chillies first, in a #mixie until you have a bright-red powder. Transfer it to a large #container.

Next, grind the roasted lentils with @salt{1%tbsp} and a little of the chilli powder. Add this to the same container.

Finally, add the coconut and curry leaves to the mixie with the @dry tamarind{1%inch piece} and @jaggery powder{3%tbsp}, along with a spoonful of the ground lentils. The lentil powder absorbs some of the oil released by the coconut and helps the mixture remain dry.

Pulse only once or twice — we want a coarse, grainy texture, not a fine powder.

Mix all three ground mixtures thoroughly. Taste and adjust the @salt{} or jaggery before storing it in a clean, dry #jar.

Best eaten with rice and dal or curd rice. It goes great with dosas and idlis as well.
